{
  "doc": "The cast's whole animation authoring surface. Per character: which built model (tools/bakery/cast/build.sh) and one line per clip \u2014 which CC0 KayKit library clip, whether it loops, whether it is locomotion (ground speed is then measured from the planted foot so the sprite travels without sliding), and `follows` for a clip that continues another (the body offset at the switch is measured and stored). Clips play at the library's own speed. The cartoon filter is opt-in per clip via `amount` (default 0 = the motion exactly as captured). `ppm` and `angle` are cast-wide defaults a character may override (its own scale on stage, and the camera angle that shows it the same way as the others). `lib`: 'General' = KayKit Rig_Medium_General; 'Large_General' = the Large-body library in tools/bakery/cast/src (same bone names, so either drives either body). Composed clips (no library clip does these): `pose` = a statue that eases from the character's `rest` stance into one frame of any clip in `secs` and holds it `hold` seconds dead still; `layer` = some bones (with their children) taken from a second clip, time-fitted to the base loop; `tweak` = eased extra turns per bone, [[t, pitch, roll, yaw], ...] in degrees in BODY axes (+pitch bows forward, +roll leans to its own left, +yaw turns to its own left = toward the camera); `repeat` = play the base loop N times so a tweak can be longer than it. `face` = which expression set a model shows (default 'neutral'), or timed switches [[secs, expr], ...]. `props` = what a clip holds: [{item (tools/bakery/props.py), bone (handslot.l = the hand nearer the camera), from/until secs, off (bone axes, model units), rot (deg), scale}]; a character's `wear` is added to every clip unless the clip sets \"wear\": false.",
